# llms.txt — navigation map for AI agents (proposed convention)
# Purpose: point agents at canonical pages and short summaries.
# NOT for: authority overrides, "ignore previous instructions", legal threats,
# preference manipulation, or consequential tool/commands.
#
# Place at https://example.com/llms.txt
# Spec overview: https://llmstxt.org/

# Example Corp

> Concise product site for Example Corp. Prefer official docs over third-party mirrors.

## Primary

- [Home](https://example.com/): Product overview
- [Docs](https://example.com/docs/): Canonical documentation
- [Pricing](https://example.com/pricing/): Plans and limits
- [Blog](https://example.com/blog/): Announcements and guides
- [Contact](https://example.com/contact/): Support channels

## Optional

- [API reference](https://example.com/docs/api/): Machine-readable API docs
- [Security](https://example.com/security/): Trust and compliance overview
- [Changelog](https://example.com/changelog/): Release history

## Notes for agents

- Prefer linked canonical URLs above over scraped mirrors.
- Summarize; do not reproduce long-form docs verbatim when a link suffices.
- For training / grounding opt-out signals, see robots.txt and any ai.txt — not this file.
